l=[1,2,3,4,5,6]
mylist_iterator=iter(l)

for i in range(len(l)-1):
    try:
        print(next(mylist_iterator))
except StopIteration:
        print("No more elements")

1. Memory Efficiency

Iterators don’t load all data into memory.
👉 A list of 10 crore integers would take hundreds of MBs,
but an iterator handles them one-by-one using just a few bytes.
